PRIVACY POLICY FOR BALIJA APP
Last Updated: January 4, 2026
Effective Date: January 4, 2026

INTRODUCTION
Balija App ("we," "our," or "us") is a community platform that connects members of the Balija community through events, business listings, and professional networking. This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard your information when you use our mobile application. We are committed to protecting your privacy and handling your data responsibly.

By downloading or using the app, you agree to the collection and use of information in accordance with this policy. If you do not agree with the terms of this Privacy Policy, please do not access the application.

INFORMATION WE COLLECT

We collect information that you provide directly to us and information automatically collected when you use the app:

1. Personal Information You Provide:
   - Account Information: Email address, name, phone number, and password (encrypted)
   - Profile Information: Business details, professional information, bio, and profile photos
   - Location Data: City, state, district, and country for location-based services
   - Content: Events, business listings, service information, photos, and community interactions

2. Automatically Collected Information:
   - Device Information: Device model, operating system version, unique device identifiers
   - Usage Data: App interactions, features used, time spent, and navigation patterns
   - Log Data: IP address, browser type, access times, and pages viewed
   - Crash Reports: Technical diagnostics and error logs for app stability
   - Analytics: Firebase Analytics for app performance and user engagement metrics

3. Location Information:
   - We collect location data only when you explicitly provide it (city, state selection)
   - We DO NOT collect precise GPS location or track your real-time location
   - Location is used only for filtering events and businesses in your area

4. Photos and Media:
   - Profile pictures and business images you upload
   - We request storage permission only for uploading photos
   - We DO NOT access your photo library without your explicit action

HOW WE USE YOUR INFORMATION

We use the collected information for the following purposes:
- To create, maintain, and secure your account
- To display your profile and business card to other community members (with your consent)
- To show relevant events and businesses based on your selected location
- To enable communication and networking within the Balija community
- To send push notifications about events, updates, and community activities (you can opt-out)
- To improve app performance, fix bugs, and enhance user experience
- To analyze app usage patterns and generate anonymous statistics
- To prevent fraud, abuse, and ensure platform safety
- To comply with legal obligations and protect our rights

DATA SHARING AND DISCLOSURE

We respect your privacy and DO NOT sell, rent, or trade your personal information.

Information Shared Within the App:
- Your profile information is visible to other app users based on your privacy settings
- Business listings and events you create are publicly visible within the app
- Your business card details are shared when you choose to display them

Third-Party Service Providers:
We share information with trusted third-party services that help us operate the app:
- Firebase (Google LLC): Authentication, push notifications, crash reporting, and analytics
- Supabase (Supabase Inc.): Database storage and file hosting for images
- Vercel (Vercel Inc.): API hosting and backend infrastructure

These providers have their own privacy policies and are required to protect your data.

Legal Requirements:
We may disclose your information if required by law, court order, legal process, or to:
- Comply with legal obligations
- Protect our rights, property, or safety
- Prevent fraud or security issues
- Respond to government requests

Business Transfers:
If we are involved in a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets, your information may be transferred. We will notify you before your information becomes subject to a different privacy policy.

YOUR RIGHTS AND CHOICES

You have the following rights regarding your personal information:

Access and Portability:
- View all personal data we hold about you
- Request a copy of your data in a portable format

Correction and Update:
- Update or correct your profile information at any time through the app

Deletion:
- Delete your account and all associated data through the app settings
- Request complete data deletion by contacting us

Privacy Controls:
- Control who can view your profile and business card
- Manage business listing visibility
- Choose what information to share

Notification Preferences:
- Opt-out of push notifications in app settings
- Control email notification preferences

Marketing Communications:
- Unsubscribe from promotional emails at any time
- We do not send unsolicited marketing messages

To exercise any of these rights, contact us through the app's support section or email.

DATA SECURITY

We take the security of your personal information seriously and implement industry-standard measures:

Technical Safeguards:
- End-to-end encrypted data transmission using HTTPS/TLS
- Firebase Authentication with secure password hashing
- Protected database with role-based access controls
- Secure API endpoints with authentication tokens
- Regular security audits and updates

Organizational Measures:
- Limited employee access to personal data
- Staff training on data protection
- Incident response procedures

However, no method of transmission over the internet or electronic storage is 100% secure. While we strive to protect your information, we cannot guarantee absolute security.

You are responsible for:
- Keeping your password confidential
- Not sharing your account credentials
- Logging out on shared devices
- Reporting any unauthorized access immediately

THIRD-PARTY SERVICES

Our app integrates with the following third-party services:

1. Firebase (Google LLC)
   - Authentication and user management
   - Push notifications (Firebase Cloud Messaging)
   - Crash reporting (Firebase Crashlytics)
